# 23-SEC / bot and agent security

**Goes here.** Detecting and stopping automated abuse of the store and the ad
accounts. Card testing, credential stuffing and account takeover, scalping, discount
and referral abuse, gift card brute forcing, scraping, fake accounts and review spam,
click fraud, bot traffic polluting analytics, and layer 7 flooding. Plus the defences,
and the monitoring that tells you an attack is running.

## The thing that makes this module different in 2026

You no longer want to block all automated traffic. Some of it is your distribution. An
answer engine crawling your specification tables is how you get cited, and an AI
shopping assistant completing a purchase for a customer is a real order. Blanket bot
blocking kills your GEO strategy and turns away buyers.

**So the job is not "block bots". It is telling wanted agents from unwanted ones, and
treating them differently.**

## The gap this folder has

The sources collected so far are general ecommerce security: threats, admin hygiene,
best practices. That is commodity knowledge. **None yet addresses wanted versus
unwanted agents**, and the `agents /` topic family is empty. That is the priority.

Look for: verified crawler and agent identification, agent allowlists, robots and
agent directives, handling agentic checkout, and how answer-engine crawlers identify
themselves versus how scrapers disguise themselves.

## Not here

- Which crawlers to attract and citation strategy -> 16-AEO
- What a chargeback costs and how reserves work -> 20-FIN
- Defining which metrics are correct -> 06-MEA
- Amazon account health -> 22-AMZ
- Store configuration and SSL setup -> 05-SET
